messages.content:
Analyze the Jira bug report title and description and the seed changes that were made to fix the reported bug. Combine this analysis with the initial static impact set, which contains the fully qualified names of code entities that are statically related to the seed changes.
For each entity in the initial static impact set, analyze its relationship to the seed changes and collect evidence indicating whether the entity must be modified as a consequence of the seed changes.  Furthermore, identify any additional code entities that must be modified or created and collect supporting evidence.
Focus on production code, not test code or other files.
Inputs: - Jira bug report title: setTextValue in DMLConfig is not behaving correctly - Jira bug report description: The problem was discovered when trying to set a configuration property from MLContext.
Specifically, it was to try and restrict which GPU to use for the program. Currently this is done via a System property.

This was the script:
{code}
unet = Caffe2DML(spark, solver='solver.prototxt', input_shape=img_shape)
unet.setGPU(True)
unet.setForceGPU(True)
unet.setConfigProperty("systemml.stats.extraGPU", "true")
unet.setConfigProperty("systemml.gpu.availableGPUs", "1")
{code}


Here is what I discovered:
The first time [setText|https://github.com/apache/systemml/blob/master/src/main/java/org/apache/sysml/conf/DMLConfig.java#L266] value is called on an empty DMLConfig (by calling new DMLConfig()) as opposed to by parsing a file, a new _xmlRoot is initialized.

Thereafter, since the _xmlRoot is not null, it tries to call getElementsByTagName, even when the tag is different. In the example above, the tag is {{systemml.stats.extraGPU"}} the first time around and {{systemml.gpu.availableGPUs}} the second time around.

The bug is in [setText|https://github.com/apache/systemml/blob/master/src/main/java/org/apache/sysml/conf/DMLConfig.java#L253] - Seed changes and their Git diff hunks: [{"fqn": "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.setTextValue(java.lang.String,java.lang.String)", "git_diff_hunk": "@@ -267,6 +264,12 @@ public class DMLConfig
- if(_xmlRoot != null)
- DMLConfig.setTextValue(_xmlRoot, paramName, paramValue);
- else {
- DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
- factory.setIgnoringComments(true); //ignore XML comments
- DocumentBuilder builder;
+ if(_xmlRoot != null) {
+ NodeList list = _xmlRoot.getElementsByTagName(paramName);
+ if (list != null && list.getLength() > 0) {
+ Element elem = (Element) list.item(0);
+ elem.getFirstChild().setNodeValue(paramValue);
+ } else {
+ Node value = _document.createTextNode(paramValue);
+ Node element = _document.createElement(paramName);
+ element.appendChild(value);
+ _xmlRoot.appendChild(element);
+ }
+ } else {
@@ -274 +277 @@ public class DMLConfig
- builder = factory.newDocumentBuilder();
+ DocumentBuilder builder = getDocumentBuilder();
@@ -276,2 +279,2 @@ public class DMLConfig
- Document domTree = builder.parse(new ByteArrayInputStream(configString.getBytes("UTF-8")));
- _xmlRoot = domTree.getDocumentElement();
+ _document = builder.parse(new ByteArrayInputStream(configString.getBytes("UTF-8")));
+ _xmlRoot = _document.getDocumentElement();"}] - Initial static code change impact set: ["org.apache.sysml.api.DMLException.DMLException(java.lang.String,java.lang.Throwable)", "org.apache.sysml.api.mlcontext.MLContext.setConfigProperty(java.lang.String,java.lang.String)", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.DEFAULT_SYSTEMML_CONFIG_FILEPATH", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.DMLConfig(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.DMLConfig(java.lang.String,boolean)", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.DMLConfig(org.w3c.dom.Element)", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.LOCAL_TMP_DIR", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.LOG", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig._document", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig._fileName", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig._xmlRoot", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.clone()", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.getDocumentBuilder()", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.parseConfig()", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.parseDMLConfig(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.readConfigurationFile(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.sysml.conf.DMLConfig.setTextValue(org.w3c.dom.Element,java.lang.String,java.lang.String)", "org.apache.sysml.runtime.DMLRuntimeException.DMLRuntimeException(java.lang.String,java.lang.Exception)"]

Expected output:
Structured evidence for each entity of the initial static impact set, including: - its fully qualified name - an assessment of whether it must be modified as a consequence of the seed changes - the supporting evidence
Additionally, include any code entities that must be modified or created but are not part of the initial static impact set.
